From 0f9d33386825ec37bd5cdf6d2f3df6a1c0693ecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:08:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sync): support ':'-separated CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR list for
 multi-account cache

Extend cache sync to ingest sessions from multiple Claude config roots in one
pass, with each session stamped by its owning root. Enables expectations design
to query work and personal sessions together without looping.

Condition 1 (labeling): every synced session carries `path.meta.claude_config_dir`
(the owning config root) and `path.meta.account` (derived from the root dir name).

Condition 2 (default unchanged): single-value or unset CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR still
works (reads one dir or ~/.claude); paths without a separator treat the value as
a literal.

Condition 3 (evaluator discipline): sync reads all roots; single-session commands
(derive, resume) read only the first, so account discipline requires evaluators
to set CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR explicitly per account (cross-account queries are a shell
and Allie feature, not a multi-account privilege). Documented in providers.rs.

Changes:
- Config.claude_config_dirs() splits $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR on ':' (platform path
  separator); empty entries dropped.
- ClaudeSource now enumerates all managers and derives with the owning manager.
- Tests: two fixtures with `:` and single-value lists; one prefix-bleed test for
  --project-under with seats named work-home, work-home-author, work-home2-author.

Fixes: path query --source claude --project-under ~/.local/state/lobby-seats
returns empty when $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR points at fleet-work but TOOLPATH_CONFIG_DIR
is on a different machine or cache; now syncs from all listed roots and labels
which account owns each session.

Decided by recommendation (consultant), local only, no push.
